Third-party protocols (interoperated with, not included)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Appia is a user interface. It composes calls to third-party Solana programs
via their public on-chain interfaces (program IDs, instruction/account layouts)
and to public cross-chain transport. It does NOT contain, fork, or redistribute
the source of any of these protocols; each remains the property of its authors
and is governed by its own license and trademarks:

  Marinade (liquid staking) · Mango (lending/borrowing) · Meteora (DAMM swaps) ·
  Wormhole · Circle CCTP.

Program IDs and chain metadata are sourced from the public
@rome-protocol/registry package.

